WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.870
A truck is bringing supplies

2
00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:03.170
to our village school.

3
00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.990
It can carry a thousand kilos, but

4
00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:08.430
the school needs more than that.

5
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.200
So what should go on the truck?

6
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.900
Today: pack the truck, and

7
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.460
find the best load.

8
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.340
Every packing puzzle has

9
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:20.960
a rule and a goal.

10
00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:24.310
The rule: no more than a thousand kilos.

11
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:28.560
The goal: the most points, because points

12
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.040
show how much the school needs each thing.

13
00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:34.110
Solar panels weigh six hundred

14
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.210
kilos, and give forty-two points.

15
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:39.900
Desks and books weigh five hundred each.

16
00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:42.490
They give thirty-three and

17
00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:43.490
thirty-two points.

18
00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.790
Then there’s a water filter,

19
00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.290
footballs, and chalk and paper.

20
00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:50.600
Here’s a quick way.

21
00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.910
First, load the thing with the most points

22
00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:55.730
for its weight: the solar panels.

23
00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.140
Then only the water filter

24
00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.520
and the chalk still fit.

25
00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:01.130
That’s sixty points.

26
00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:02.870
Quick check!

27
00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:05.230
The solar panels are on the

28
00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:07.190
truck: six hundred kilos.

29
00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:09.550
Can the desks, five

30
00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:11.070
hundred kilos, go on too?

31
00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.470
No: six hundred and five

32
00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:16.350
hundred make eleven hundred.

33
00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:17.950
That’s too heavy.

34
00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:20.750
A load that breaks the rule doesn’t

35
00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.810
count, however many points it has.

36
00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.970
Now try the desks and the books.

37
00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:28.710
Five hundred and five hundred

38
00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.750
make exactly a thousand.

39
00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:34.570
And thirty-three and thirty-two make

40
00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:37.010
sixty-five points, more than sixty!

41
00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:40.530
So the quick way wasn’t the best.

42
00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:43.250
The best load has the most points

43
00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:45.110
and still keeps the rule.

44
00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.520
With six loads, there are sixty-four ways

45
00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:51.020
to pack, so you can check them all.

46
00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.120
Something always stays behind.

47
00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:56.730
This time, it’s the solar panels.

48
00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:58.250
Who decides?

49
00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:00.870
Could they come on the next trip?

50
00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:04.490
In the app, tap loads to put

51
00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:05.370
them on the truck yourself.

52
00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.360
Watch the weight, and count your points.

53
00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:10.990
Then press Show the best

54
00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:12.350
load, and compare.

55
00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:14.180
Your turn.

56
00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:17.310
Your load is the desks and the

57
00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:19.670
water filter: eight hundred kilos

58
00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:21.490
and forty-eight points.

59
00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.290
Is it the best load?

60
00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:27.580
No: it keeps the rule, but the desks

61
00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.860
and the books give sixty-five.

62
00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.040
Remember: keep the rule

63
00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.900
first, then chase the goal.

64
00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:36.820
Quick ways are good, but check them.

65
00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.580
And think about what stays behind.

66
00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.870
Try it yourself: pack your

67
00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.370
school bag like a truck.

68
00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.210
Give each thing a weight and

69
00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:49.170
points, and choose a limit.

70
00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:51.720
Find the load with the most points,

71
00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:54.440
then ask a friend to beat it.
